  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The circuit images did not render, so the layout is built from the circuit text. Rail 'tp' is used as 5V and rail 'tn' as GND.",
   "Each FSR has one leg in the 5V rail and the other in its own column. That column holds the analog wire (A0, A1 or A2) and one leg of a 10k pull-down resistor. The resistor's other leg goes to the GND rail. This gives three parallel FSR dividers.",
   "Pin 8 goes through a wire to a column, then through the 100 ohm resistor to the speaker. The speaker's other terminal goes to the GND rail. The speaker is not polarised, so which terminal goes where does not matter.",
   "Each physical connection has a joined edge and an electrical edge on the same ports."
